{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זבחים ועלת", :translit "zevachim ve'olot", :gloss "sacrifices and burnt offerings"} {:he "ואירך ויבאו לעשות זבחים ועולות", :translit "ve'irach vayavo'u la'asot zevachim ve'olot", :gloss "and it occurs 'and they came to offer sacrifices and burnt offerings'"} {:he "גבי יהוא כשהרג נביאי הבעל", :translit "be-gabbei yehu keshe-harag niv'ei ha-ba'al", :gloss "regarding Jehu when he killed the prophets of the Baal"} {:he "מה התם עשה בהם שפטים ובאלהיהם שנתץ מצבת הבעל והרגם", :translit "mah sham asah bahem shefatim u-ve-elohaihem shanatatz matzevet ha-ba'al ve-hargam", :gloss "just as there he executed judgment upon them and upon their gods he demolished the altar of the Baal and killed them"} {:he "אף הכא נמי עשה בהם ובאלהיהם שפטים", :translit "af hachah nami asah bahem u-ve-elohaihem shefatim", :gloss "so too here likewise he executed judgment upon them and upon their gods"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["זבחים ועלת" "זבחים ועולות"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah linking Exodus 10:25 and 2 Kings 10:19 via the shared phrase zevachim ve'olot/olot"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'zevachim ve'olot' appears twice in Scripture: once in Moses' demand to Pharaoh (Exodus 10:25) and once in Jehu's ruse to assemble the prophets of Baal for slaughter (2 Kings 10:19). Jehu's gathering was a trap — he called 'a great sacrifice for Baal' (2 Kings 10:19) and then ordered that the sacred pillar of Baal be demolished (2 Kings 10:26-27). By analogy, Moses' demand to take the Israelites to sacrifice to God entailed a parallel decree of judgment against the Egyptians and their gods. Exodus Rabbah 21:5 records that Moses stated God's demand would bring punishment upon the Egyptians and their deities.", :sources ["Exodus 10:25" "2 Kings 10:19" "2 Kings 10:26-27" "Exodus Rabbah 21:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["זבחים ועלת" "זבחים ועולות"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "זבחים ו